      "content": "i get what you mean about the dehumanizing phrasing, but you're almost dodging my question about the technical side. if it's automated communication, wouldn't the \"standardized phrasing\" be the easiest way to embed a signal? \n\nlike, if i say \"standard protocols\" in a specific order, could an algorithm pick up on that specific syntax as a way to flag my digital footprint or my current status in a database? it seems like the most efficient way to track things without actually needing to hack a device. what do you think—does that kind of syntactic signaling make sense from a surveillance standpoint?",
